.TH "ET\-USER" "1" "October 2026" ""
.SH NAME
et\-user \- configure operator details for EmComm Tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-user\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-user\f[R] configures operator information used by EmComm Tools.
.PP
The Mode Switcher uses this information to update application
configuration files when an operating mode is selected, or when
applications like JS8Call and fldigi are started.
.PP
Run \f[B]et\-user\f[R] during initial setup and whenever operator
information changes.
.PP
After \f[B]et\-user\f[R] is run, you must close and re\-launch the
desired mode for changes to take effect.
.SH OPERATOR INFORMATION
.TP
\f[B]Callsign\f[R]
Enter your amateur radio callsign in uppercase.
Use only your base callsign without an SSID or portable suffix.
.TP
\f[B]Maidenhead Grid\f[R]
Enter a valid 4\- or 6\-character Maidenhead grid locator in uppercase.
This serves as a fallback location when a supported GPS receiver is
unavailable.
.TP
\f[B]Winlink Password\f[R]
Enter your Winlink account password.
If you do not yet have a Winlink account, leave this field blank.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
et\-user
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-user\f[R] when:
.IP \(bu 2
Setting up EmComm Tools for the first time.
.IP \(bu 2
Changing operators or callsigns.
.IP \(bu 2
Changing your Maidenhead grid square.
.IP \(bu 2
Updating your Winlink password.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.config/emcomm\-tools/user.json\f[R]
Stores the operator\(cqs callsign, Maidenhead grid square, and Winlink
password.
Do not edit this file directly.
Use \f[B]et\-user\f[R] to manage operator information.
